  "target_summary": {
    "source_message_id": 309,
    "speaker": "client",
    "text": "Either option is acceptable: remove the 44Ω resistors if they complicate the layout, or leave them in place if they are already fitted and not obstructing anything.\n\nThose resistors on SDA/SCL are only there for signal quality. Because I2C lines are open-drain, releasing them requires the pull-up resistor to recharge the cable capacitance to 3.3V. That can produce slight overshoot or ringing at the transition edge, which the series resistance damps.\n\nWith our 20–40cm cables and 4.4kΩ pull-ups, rise time will remain well within specification, so this should not be a meaningful problem."
  },
